Patch 0002-fp8-dense-and-draft-vocab.patch for vLLM, base commit 77154ca6116ae34cbfe314beef1016bde9b63989 (vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-77154ca6116ae34cbfe314beef1016bde9b63989).
What: QWEN38_FP8_DENSE casts the checkpoint's BF16 dense linears (GDN, QSA, shared experts, MTP dense, lm_head) to 128x128 block FP8 at load (197 linears); QWEN4EXP_DRAFT_VOCAB limits MTP drafting to token ids below 65,536; keeps the QSA indexer projection unfused so its rows stay BF16.
Upstream: no vLLM PR. FP8-dense cast and indexer handling written for this recipe; the reduced-vocabulary drafting ports tonyd2wild's mtp_draft_vocab.py (Tony DeAngelo, Tech2Wild / 2Wild, Apache-2.0; https://github.com/tonyd2wild/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4-DGX-Spark @ 6ad1c8f), credited in the code as 'Kai / 2Wild'.
This file modifies vLLM (Apache-2.0); the vLLM copyright and SPDX lines in the files it changes are kept.

